I verified the root cause and the fix, and pushed two additions.

Revert-verified the `ScreenWriter` change on its own, keeping the `ScreenBuffer` scrollback support so the signal was clean: all five new cases fail on 8.1 with an empty scrollback where `L0..L3` is expected. #65966's own tests are untouched by this and still pass, so the narrower guard does not give its symptom back. Full Tui suite green at 1815.

The line feed is safe on the column: `$buffer .= "\r"` already follows the motion, so a terminal in newline mode cannot shift the starting column.

**`scrollUp()` could push `null` into the scrollback.** `array_shift()` returns `null` on an empty array, and `clear()` leaves `$this->cells` empty when the terminal reports zero rows, so `getScrollback()` then died:

```
new ScreenBuffer(20, 0), write("a\nb\nc\n")
  TypeError: ScreenBuffer::renderCells(): Argument #1 ($cells) must be of type array, null given
```

This is what Psalm was reporting as `InvalidPropertyAssignmentValue` at `ScreenBuffer.php:394`, so the red check was a real defect rather than an annotation gap. Fixed with `?? []` and covered by `testScrollbackOfAZeroHeightBuffer`, which fails with exactly that `TypeError` without the fix. I also added `testErasingTheScrollbackDropsTheLinesThatScrolledOff`, which protects the new `ED 3` behaviour rather than proving the fix.

Fabbot stays red on a pre-existing line: `RenderException`'s `Line preview: %s%s` comes from `a81867921ed [Tui] Add the component` and this PR does not touch it. The check lints whole touched files, so any PR touching `ScreenWriter.php` inherits it, as #65966 did before merging. I left it alone rather than fold an unrelated message change in here.

I recorded the 8.2 resolution in the description: `ScreenWriter.php` conflicts there, and the new test merges cleanly and then fails, because 8.2 has no `writeLines()`.
